  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-17T17:29:51.662Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As of now to find my group you have to type 3 full words for it to show up.  I suggest two things: add keywords as a way to help people find groups of a specific type and allow people to search for groups via short or partial queiries.\n\n For example, if a group is called The Cat Club, typing Cat Club will not yield results. \n\n With my suggestion the term cat or club could find the group.  Furthermore, the words feline, animal, kitten, kat etc. could be used as key words set by the group creator.\n\nAs of now the system is encouraging people to use incredibly vague one word topics as names instead of fleshing out their group name so people can find it organically.  This feature would drastically reduce the need to spam people with group invites to grow a group and make search much more useful for discovering new groups without knowing the name beforehand.",
